  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: Three completed experiments establish that RNA (PCA n2000) is the dominant signal source (0.485 acc) while image alone is weak (0.208 acc), and adding ResNet50 image via concat yields a modest +4.2 pt multimodal gain (0.527). The RNA encoder has only been tested as linear PCA, which is a very simple baseline. Uncertainty: It is entirely unknown whether a learned RNA representation (scvi, scGPT) substantially outperforms PCA for the dominant modality. This is the highest-impact unexplored axis because the RNA encoder choice will propagate to every future multimodal configuration. Question: config_004 (RNA-only, single profile, scvi_n200) changes exactly one variable relative to config_001 (PCA n2000 → scvi n200), cleanly isolating the effect of a learned latent representation versus linear dimensionality reduction. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a minimal, single-variable comparison that reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental design choice (RNA representation quality) before investing budget in more complex multimodal, multiprofile, or fusion variants. If scvi substantially improves over PCA, it justifies exploring scvi-based multimodal configs; if it does not, PCA remains the preferred encoder and we can focus budget on other axes (multiprofile, image encoder, fusion). This is more informative than testing fusion strategy or image encoder, which affect a weaker modality, and more informative than multiprofile configs, which change two variables simultaneously (profile setting + aggregation)."
}

